{
  "note": "Pinned open-source projects built with rkp (tools/run-corpus.mjs). Each entry is a repository at one commit; `build` is the rkp command line run in `dir`; `expect` says what a good build looks like. `installArgs` adds options to `pnpm install` (`--trust-lockfile` skips pnpm's supply-chain check of a lockfile it distrusts); `dropLockfile` resolves versions afresh when the project's lockfile is in a format this pnpm cannot read, so that project is not pinned past its commit. `dir` is a folder of a larger repository (only it is fetched). The `vite-template-*` projects have no lockfile, so their dependencies are resolved when the run happens: a failure in one may come from a newer release of a dependency, not only from rkp. `kind: cli` is a program built for Node: `expect.run` runs the output with the given arguments and matches what it prints. `expectFail` records a known gap with its reason: the run shows it as expected, and flags it when it starts to pass.",
